  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Chariots of Fire**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Pretty Girl**: rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Cumberland Blues (tease)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2018-10-17.MK012aud** (recommended): audience recording; 27 songs; 152 min [1]\n- **ween2018-10-17.CMC44-2448**: source not stated; 25 songs; 151 min; rated 3/5 by 1 [3]\n- **Ween2018-10-17.AK40.FLAC**: source not stated; 27 songs; 151 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- A drunk woman stood on her seat for the second half of one song, booing, calling it insensitive and flipping off the band [1]\n- The whole show was played with Bobby Ogdin and the Shit Creek Boys [1]\n- The show was billed as Ween and the Shit Creek Boys [3]\n- The taper had made a well-regarded audience tape of the Shit Creek Boys at the Fillmore in 1996 [4]\n- This was the second night; a separate recording of the first night, October 16, is also on the Archive [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2018-10-17.MK012aud**: taped by Zachariah Boes; source: Oktava MK-012-01 (cards) > Fostex FR-2LE (24/48) [1]. Also: Taped and transferred by Zachariah Boes using Oktava MK-012-01 cardioid mics into a Fostex FR2-LE at 24-bit/48k [1]\n- **ween2018-10-17.CMC44-2448**: source: Schoeps CMC44's > Groade capacitor supply > Edirol R-09HR > WAV (48kHz/24 bit) [3]. Also: Recorded from an upstairs seat off center at the Ryman; Captain Fireball uploaded and labeled it for the taper's account [4]\n- **Ween2018-10-17.AK40.FLAC**: taped by Melissa Fry; transferred by Melissa Fry; source: Neumann AK40> Oade m248> Sound Devices 722 [2]",
